examples.css:
.card { max-width: 300px; padding: 16px; border: 2px solid #e2e8f0; border-radius: 10px; font-family: sans-serif; }
.card--featured { border-color: gold; background: #fffbeb; }
.card__title { margin: 0 0 6px; font-size: 18px; }
.card__text { margin: 0 0 12px; color: #475569; }
.btn { display: inline-block; padding: 6px 12px; background: #2965f1; color: #fff; text-decoration: none; border-radius: 6px; }
.btn--large { padding: 10px 22px; font-size: 16px; }

.flex { display: flex; } .gap-2 { gap: .5rem; } .p-4 { padding: 1rem; }
.rounded { border-radius: 10px; } .bg-slate { background: #e2e8f0; } .bg-blue { background: #2965f1 !important; color: #fff; }
.chip { background: #fff; padding: 4px 10px; border-radius: 999px; font: 13px sans-serif; }

.lane { width: 100%; height: 36px; background: #e2e8f0; margin-bottom: 6px; position: relative; }
.ball { width: 30px; height: 30px; margin: 3px; border-radius: 50%; position: absolute; left: 0; }
.good { background: #16a34a; animation: moveT 2s ease-in-out infinite alternate; will-change: transform; }
.bad { background: #e11d48; animation: moveM 2s ease-in-out infinite alternate; }
@keyframes moveT { to { transform: translateX(260px); } }
@keyframes moveM { to { left: 260px; } }
.note { font: 12px sans-serif; color: #475569; }

* { outline: 1px solid rgba(220, 38, 38, .6); }
.a { padding: 12px; font-family: sans-serif; }
.b { width: 80px; margin: 10px 0; }
/* the outline does not change layout, so you can see every box */

.parent { background: #fde68a; font-family: sans-serif; }
.child { margin-top: 40px; background: #fff; }
/* fix: .parent { display: flow-root; } or padding-top: 1px */

topics.description:
CSS decisions directly affect accessibility.

### Focus styles
Keyboard users need to see where they are. Never remove outlines without a replacement.

```css
:focus-visible { outline: 3px solid #2965f1; outline-offset: 3px; }
```
`:focus-visible` shows rings for keyboard use only.

### Contrast
WCAG AA: **4.5:1** for normal text, **3:1** for large text and UI components. Check with DevTools color picker.

### Respect user preferences
```css
@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
  *, *::before, *::after {
    animation-duration: .01ms !important;
    animation-iteration-count: 1 !important;
    transition-duration: .01ms !important;
    scroll-behavior: auto !important;
  }
}
@media (prefers-contrast: more) { :root { --border: #000; } }
@media (forced-colors: active) { .btn { border: 1px solid ButtonText; } }
```

### Visually hidden text (sr-only)
```css
.sr-only { position: absolute; width: 1px; height: 1px; margin: -1px; padding: 0;
  overflow: hidden; clip: rect(0 0 0 0); white-space: nowrap; border: 0; }
```

### Other points
- Use **rem** so text can scale; do not disable zoom.
- Do not rely on color alone (add icons/text).
- Tap targets >= 44x44px.
- `display: none` / `visibility: hidden` hide from assistive tech; opacity does not.
- Do not put important text in `::before` content.
- Keep line-height >= 1.5 for body text.

examples.css:
.btn { font-size: 20px; padding: 8px 14px; border: 2px solid #0f172a; background: #fff; border-radius: 8px; }
.btn:focus-visible, .link:focus-visible { outline: 3px solid #2965f1; outline-offset: 3px; }
.link { font: 16px sans-serif; margin-left: 12px; }
.sr-only { position: absolute; width: 1px; height: 1px; margin: -1px; overflow: hidden; clip: rect(0 0 0 0); white-space: nowrap; border: 0; }

.m { width: 120px; padding: 12px; background: #7c3aed; color: #fff; font: 13px sans-serif; animation: slide 1.4s ease-in-out infinite alternate; }
@keyframes slide { to { transform: translateX(160px); } }
@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { .m { animation: none; } }
